      22["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Health function</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Vercel Function (Node.js)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Public GET /api/health<br />returning ok and the short<br />commit SHA, with no caching<br />and no other data.</div>"]
      style 22 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#444444,color:#444444
      23["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Worker function</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Vercel Function (Node.js, 300 s)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>POST<br />/api/jobs/process/[jobId]:<br />verifies the QStash signature<br />against APP_BASE_URL plus the<br />path and the raw body, runs<br />one tick of one job<br />(serverless Chromium for the<br />export trigger; one<br />supervisor decision on a<br />pending incident, from a<br />closed set of actions with<br />deterministic preconditions),<br />publishes the next wakeup,<br />and records the _ping smoke<br />test's nonce.</div>"]
      style 23 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#444444,color:#444444
      24["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Daily cron function</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Vercel Function (Node.js, 300 s, Vercel Cron)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>GET /api/cron/daily with the<br />cron secret: auto-start when<br />enabled, the watchdog and<br />lifetime check, Google, Drive<br />and Notion probes, login<br />warnings, resuming a job<br />whose login works again, and<br />the heartbeat; ?probe= runs<br />one probe.</div>"]
      style 24 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#444444,color:#444444
      25["<div style='font-weight: bold'>MCP function</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Vercel Function (Node.js, MCP Streamable HTTP)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>POST /mcp (rewritten to<br />/api/mcp) with the bearer<br />token, an Origin rule and an<br />hourly limit: a new stateless<br />MCP server per request with 7<br />tools (start, status, list,<br />process, retry, cancel,<br />health) whose views come from<br />an allowlist; it publishes<br />wakeups and never runs a<br />step. backup_health with<br />checkAgent runs one canned,<br />content-free supervisor<br />decision.</div>"]
      style 25 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#444444,color:#444444
      26["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Telegram integration function</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Vercel Function (Node.js)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>POST<br />/api/integrations/telegram<br />with the integration bearer<br />token: normalized commands<br />and callbacks from the hub,<br />backup action deduplication<br />and single-use confirmations;<br />status, retry, cancel and<br />login guidance use the<br />existing backup application<br />methods.</div>"]
      style 26 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#444444,color:#444444
      27["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Local CLI</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Node.js + TypeScript CLI + Playwright]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>auth:google, auth:notion,<br />drive:check, drive:init,<br />doctor, smoke:qstash,<br />dev:upload, dev:trigger,<br />dev:download, dev:tick, and<br />telegram:setup: Google<br />consent, a Notion sign-in you<br />complete in a Chrome window<br />that then resumes a job<br />waiting for it, the deployed<br />QStash smoke test, trusted<br />export-email discovery, Drive<br />probes, Redis/session<br />diagnostics,<br />checksum-verified test<br />uploads into the _dev folder,<br />dev-session export requests<br />and download checks, the<br />whole dev backup job one tick<br />per call, and Telegram test<br />notifications through the<br />independent hub; bot setup is<br />owned by the hub CLI.</div>"]
      style 27 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#444444,color:#444444
      28["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Local configuration</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: .env.local file]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Google OAuth credentials and<br />refresh token, the Telegram<br />hub URL, integration ID and<br />bearer token, plus connection<br />and encryption settings; no<br />bot token or webhook<br />configuration.</div>"]
